+# ArbiLend — Security Review
+
+**Scope:** `src/` at commit `fb2a9c4` — `LendingMarket.sol`, `CollateralVault.sol`,
+`PriceOracle.sol`, `MarketProxy.sol`, interfaces. Target chain: Arbitrum One.
+**Method:** manual review. No test suite exists, so nothing here is backed by a
+failing test — every finding is read off the source and hand-traced.
+
+**Bottom line: do not deploy this.** Five findings are individually fatal. Three of
+them (C-1, C-2, C-3) let *any* address take the entire market in a single
+transaction, and C-4 means the market liquidates honest users under completely
+normal operation. This is not a "fix the top of the list" situation; the borrow /
+health / liquidation path needs to be rewritten and then tested.
+
+---
+
+## Ranked findings
+
+| # | Severity | Location | Issue |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| C-1 | Critical | `LendingMarket.upgradeTo` | No access control — anyone can replace the implementation |
+| C-2 | Critical | `LendingMarket.setOracle` | No access control — anyone can swap in a fake oracle |
+| C-3 | Critical | `LendingMarket.setLiquidationThreshold` | No access control — anyone can set LT arbitrarily |
+| C-4 | Critical | `LendingMarket.healthFactor` | Division before multiplication — solvent users are liquidatable |
+| C-5 | Critical | `LendingMarket.borrowWithSig` | Signature replay: no nonce, no deadline |
+| H-1 | High | `PriceOracle.getPrice` | `latestAnswer()`, no staleness / round / zero validation |
+| H-2 | High | `PriceOracle.getPrice` | No Arbitrum sequencer-uptime check |
+| H-3 | High | Oracle config (README) | wstETH priced off the **stETH/USD** feed |
+| H-4 | High | `CollateralVault.withdraw` | Transfer before state update (CEI violation) |
+| M-1 | Medium | `LendingMarket.borrow` / `liquidateAll` | `borrow(0)` griefing permanently bricks `liquidateAll` |
+| M-2 | Medium | `LendingMarket._liquidate` | No close factor — always a 100% liquidation |
+| M-3 | Medium | `LendingMarket._liquidate` / `liquidateAll` | Liquidator can be forced to absorb bad debt |
+| M-4 | Medium | `LendingMarket.accrueInterest` | Interest derived from `block.number * 12` on Arbitrum |
+| M-5 | Medium | everywhere | ERC-20 return values ignored — breaks on USDT (on the shortlist) |
+| M-6 | Medium | `CollateralVault.deposit` | Fee-on-transfer and rebasing collateral unsupported (both on the roadmap) |
+| M-7 | Medium | `LendingMarket.listCollateral` | No delisting path; one bad feed DoSes the whole market |
+| L-1 | Low | `LendingMarket.repay` | Rounding dust — a position can never be fully closed |
+| L-2 | Low | `CollateralVault.withdraw` | Health check runs against a stale borrow index |
+| L-3 | Low | `LendingMarket.initialize` | Implementation left uninitialized / initializer unguarded |
+| L-4 | Low | `LendingMarket` | No ownership transfer, no pause, no zero-address checks |
+| L-5 | Low | `LendingMarket.collateralValueUsd` | Unbounded loop over `collateralTokens` |
+| L-6 | Low | `MarketProxy` / `upgradeTo` | No codesize check, no atomic upgrade-and-call |
+| I-1 | Info | `LendingMarket.domainSeparator` | Cached at init — replayable across a chain fork |
+| I-2 | Info | deployment | `CollateralVault.market` must be the proxy; circular dependency |
